    "title": "Scottsboro city schools mourns death of student - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Taylor Mitchell No media credit provided. ,\n3 hours ago\nSCOTTSBORO, Ala. (WHNT) — Scottsboro City Schools Interim Superintendent Jason Hass says a student at Scottsboro High School has died.\nHass said on social media that the student died on Wednesday morning. He said that at the request of the student’s parents, the system waited to make a public announcement until Wednesday afternoon.\nThe interim superintendent said while the system cannot share any details about the student’s death, it plans to have staff available at the school to provide support for students and staff.\n“Our hearts are broken for the family’s loss, and we ask that the family’s privacy be respected during this difficult time,” He said. “When our school community experiences such a tragedy, it impacts all of us. Our thoughts and prayers are with the family, students, faculty, staff and community.”\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WHNT.com.\n6",
